upgrading.declarations.deprecatedClass
======================================

A class whose declaration is `@deprecated`, replaced by the class the deprecation names, reported where it names none.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · needs types · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `keep`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` .[decision-facts]


upgrading.declarations.deprecatedMember
=======================================

A constant, method or property whose declaration is `@deprecated`, replaced by the member the deprecation names, reported where it names none.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · needs types · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `keep`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` .[decision-facts]

The replacement can be a member of the same class, and for a static call also a public static method of another class; DressCode writes it the way the file can reach it and adds an import where needed. The replacement must accept the call the same way as the original method; parameter names matter only where the call passes arguments by name. But the annotation is true only for the installed version. Where the deprecated class or its replacement belongs to a package installed in a newer version than the lowest version the `composer.json` of the project allows, DressCode rewrites nothing, because the replacement may not exist in the older version, and it does not report the deprecated class or member of such a package either. To install the lowest versions into `vendor`, run `composer update --prefer-lowest`. For a package that the project does not require itself, or requires without a lower bound, the deprecated use is only reported. The fix is [risky |/configuration#risky-fixes], like every replacement based on an annotation: the annotation says what to write, not that it behaves the same, so the fix is made only with `fixRisky` or `--fix-risky`. A method called on an object whose replacement is in another class is only reported, never rewritten.

```neon
typeAnalysis: phpstan

upgrading:
	declarations:
		deprecatedMember: forbidden
```

```php .[before]
use Acme\Text\Text;

$valid = Text::check($s);  // Static method `Acme\Text\Text::check()` is deprecated: use Acme\Text\Encoding::isValid().
```

```php .[after]
use Acme\Text\Encoding;
use Acme\Text\Text;

$valid = Encoding::isValid($s);
```


upgrading.declarations.deprecatedFunction
=========================================

A function whose declaration is `@deprecated`, replaced by the function the deprecation names, reported where it names none.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · needs types · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `keep`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` .[decision-facts]


upgrading.php.deprecatedArgument
================================

An argument whose value PHP deprecated is reported, `E_USER_ERROR` given to `trigger_error()` or an integer to a `ctype_*()` function.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` .[decision-facts]


upgrading.unseen.classNameString
================================

A string holding the name of a class `replacedClasses` or `forbiddenClasses` names, which no rename of the class reaches.

- `reported`: reported where it stands: the string `'Acme\Old'` naming a class the maps rename or forbid
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `keep`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` .[decision-facts]


upgrading.unseen.dynamicAccess
==============================

A member, a class or a function reached by a name the code computes, which no map of upgrading data matches.

- `reported`: reported where it stands: `$object->$method()`, `new $class`, `call_user_func($callback)`
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `keep`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` .[decision-facts]
